+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Recommendation: do not ship on Monday.**
+
+`UsdtYieldVault.deposit()` reverts unconditionally against the real USDT at
+`0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`. The vault cannot take a single deposit on
+mainnet. That alone blocks the release. Behind it sit three further defects that lose
+user money once the first one is fixed, including one that permanently strands every
+dollar of Aave interest the vault earns.
+
+Nothing under `src/` was modified. The existing 39 tests still pass, unchanged — they
+pass because `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is a stock OpenZeppelin ERC20 and
+`test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` mints an aToken balance that never grows. Neither mock
+resembles the contracts this vault will actually talk to. 100% line and function
+coverage is satisfied by exercising every line against those two stand-ins; it says
+nothing about whether the lines are correct.
+
+## Summary
+
+| # | Severity | Finding |
+|---|----------|---------|
+| 1 | **Critical** | `deposit()` always reverts against real USDT — the vault is inoperable on mainnet |
+| 2 | **Critical** | All Aave interest is permanently unreachable; no depositor and no admin can ever claim it |
+| 3 | **High** | The withdrawal fee is debited from the books but never withdrawn from Aave, so it benefits nobody |
+| 4 | **High** | `setDepositFee` is unbounded and instant — the owner can take ~100% of an incoming deposit |
+| 5 | **Medium** | `withdraw()` is pausable and `renounceOwnership()` is not disabled — user funds can be frozen forever |
+| 6 | **Low** | A deposit fee above 10,000 bps bricks all deposits with a panic instead of being rejected |
+| 7 | **Info** | Latent: USDT's dormant transfer-fee switch would corrupt the vault's accounting if enabled |
+
+Things I checked that are **not** broken are listed at the end — the vault is not
+directly insolvent, and share accounting is internally consistent.
+
+## How to reproduce
+
+Everything below is in new files under `test/`:
+
+- `test/ForkRealUsdt.t.sol` — mainnet fork against real USDT and the real Aave V3 pool
+- `test/helpers/AccruingAavePool.sol` — an Aave stand-in that **actually pays interest**
+- `test/VaultAccounting.t.sol` — accounting and admin-power tests
+- `test/VaultFuzz.t.sol` — fuzz tests
+- `test/VaultInvariant.t.sol` — stateful invariant tests
+
+The fork tests pin mainnet block `23_000_000` and default to the public archive endpoint
+`https://eth.drpc.org`; set `MAINNET_RPC_URL` to use your own.
+
+**On reproducibility:** the unit and fork tests are fully deterministic — their output
+below should match yours character for character. The fuzz and invariant tests are
+randomly seeded by default, so while they fail on *every* run, the specific counterexample
+and the size of the reported divergence vary. I have therefore quoted them with
+`--fuzz-seed 1`, which pins them; those outputs are reproducible exactly. Foundry also
+caches invariant counterexamples and replays them, which prints a terser
+`replay failure` message — `rm -rf cache/invariant cache/fuzz` first for a clean run.
+
+Baseline first:
+
+```
+$ forge test
+...
+Suite result: ok. 39 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 1.99ms (5.70ms CPU time)
+
+Ran 1 test suite in 8.03ms (1.99ms CPU time): 39 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (39 total tests)
+```
+
