+
+## 1. Critical — `deposit()` always reverts against real USDT
+
+**The vault does not work on mainnet at all.** Not in an edge case; on the first deposit.
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:94` calls `usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount)` through the
+`IERC20` interface, which declares `approve` as returning `bool`. Real USDT predates
+ERC-20 finalisation and its `approve` **returns nothing**. Solidity's ABI decoder tries
+to read a `bool` from zero bytes of returndata and reverts.
+
+Note the asymmetry that makes this easy to miss: line 93 uses
+`usdt.safeTransferFrom(...)`, and `SafeERC20` tolerates USDT's missing return value
+perfectly. Only the raw `approve` on line 94 is unwrapped.
+
+`MockUSDT` inherits OpenZeppelin's `ERC20`, whose `approve` dutifully returns `true`, so
+all 39 existing tests sail past this line.
+
+### Evidence
+
+Confirming that mainnet USDT's `approve` returns empty returndata:
+
+```
+$ cast call 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7 "approve(address,uint256)" \
+    0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2 1000000 \
+    --from 0x5754284f345afc66a98fbB0a0Afe71e0F007B949 --rpc-url https://eth.drpc.org
+0x
+```
+
+The most basic user action, on a fork, against the real token and the real pool:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path test/ForkRealUsdt.t.sol -vv
+
+Ran 2 tests for test/ForkRealUsdt.t.sol:ForkRealUsdtTest
+[FAIL: EvmError: Revert] test_AliceCanDepositRealUsdt() (gas: 94231)
+[PASS] test_Diagnosis_UsdtApproveReturnsNoData() (gas: 41317)
+Logs:
+  raw call succeeded: true
+  returndata length : 0
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 1 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 258.28ms (705.48µs CPU time)
+```
+
+The trace pinpoints it. `transferFrom` succeeds via `SafeERC20`; `approve` returns
+`[Stop]` — no data — and `deposit` reverts on the very next opcode:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_AliceCanDepositRealUsdt -vvvv
+
+  [94231] ForkRealUsdtTest::test_AliceCanDepositRealUsdt()
+    ├─ [0] VM::prank(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6])
+    │   └─ ← [Return]
+    ├─ [84174] UsdtYieldVault::deposit(1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   ├─ [43630] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::transferFrom(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Transfer(from: alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], to: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], value: 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   ├─ [24953] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::approve(0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Approval(owner: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], spender: 0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, value: 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+    └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+```
+
+### Fix
+
+Use `SafeERC20` for the approval as well as the transfer — `usdt` is already
+`using SafeERC20 for IERC20`, so the change on line 94 is:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`forceApprove` both tolerates the missing return value and handles USDT's other quirk:
+USDT rejects a non-zero-to-non-zero `approve`, so it resets the allowance to zero first.
+That second property matters if an allowance is ever left dangling — with a plain
+`approve` the vault would be bricked until someone drained the residue.
+
+A cleaner alternative is to approve `type(uint256).max` once in the constructor and drop
+the per-deposit approval entirely, saving an `SSTORE` on every deposit.
+
+**Also add a mainnet fork test to CI.** This class of bug is undetectable against
+`MockUSDT` by construction, so no amount of unit-test coverage will catch a regression.
+
